    "teach_5": {
      "id": "teach_5",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Sometimes a share is compared with the other shares together.\n\nA = 2/5 of (B+C).\nThen 5A = 2(B+C).",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_5_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_5_step": {
      "id": "teach_5_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "If the total T=A+B+C, then B+C=T−A.\nSo A = 2/5(T−A). This turns a messy-looking condition into one equation in A.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
